---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DocSection from '../components/DocSection.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const recognition = [
  'Specialist of the Quarter (x2) and Specialist of the Year',
  'Ricoh STAR Award',
  'Microsoft Azure Fundamentals, plus multiple enterprise product certifications',
];
---

<Layout title="About · Maxfield Allison" description="Ten years working with enterprise customers. Platform design, the business case behind it, and responsibility for what happens next." ogImage="/og/about.png?v=2">
  <article class="page-shell pt-16 pb-8">
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:gap-10 md:grid-cols-[var(--rail)_minmax(0,1fr)]">
    <p class="eyebrow md:pt-5">About me</p>
    <div>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-[2.75rem] leading-tight mt-4 mb-8">Maxfield Allison</h1>
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-xl font-serif text-[var(--color-ink)]">I design enterprise infrastructure, argue for it, and then run it.</p>
      <p>I've spent ten years working with enterprise customers. Today I'm the named application owner and single global escalation point for an output-management platform on Azure. Thousands of devices depend on it across four regions. When it stops, people can't print, and in parts of that business printing isn't optional.</p>
      <p>A lot of the work happens between teams. I contributed to the architecture decisions for the move from on-premises into Azure. The network and firewall layers belong to other teams, but when a configuration fault in one of them broke DNS across the platform, I worked with the vendor and the customer's security group to get it corrected.</p>
      <p>I also made the business case for a non-production environment that mirrors production. I won the funding and defined the design, sizing, and resource requirements across three organizations. The platform teams own the provisioning. <a href="/projects/test-environment">The case study</a> gets into why getting it approved took longer than designing it.</p>
      <p>Platform-related support tickets fell 38% year over year, measured in the customer's ServiceNow, as I stabilized the operating model and pushed documentation and self-service. I'm now redesigning the account's operational data and documentation around agentic systems and Microsoft Power Automate flows.</p>
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <DocSection label="The tools" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">How I work with AI</h2>
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      <p>I direct AI agents and own the engineering. I set the architecture and acceptance criteria, review what comes back, and send it back when it doesn't hold up. With dnsweaver, that means I own the design and releases while agents implement the code. I'm responsible for what I put out under my name.</p>
      <p>The useful part is how much more I can investigate and review. I can follow an alternative far enough to understand why it won't work, or have a proposed change challenged before I accept it. That still requires me to understand the system and decide what evidence is enough. I've written more about <a href="https://probablyfine.dev/blog/how-i-use-ai?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=about" data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">how I use AI</a>, including the limits of my own process.</p>
    </div>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection label="At home" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">I like having a project to work on</h2>
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      <p>The homelab started as a way to watch movies. Now there's Kubernetes, a Proxmox cluster with Ceph underneath, and a collection of services and tools that keeps giving me something else to figure out. Some of what I learn there turns out to be useful at work. I'd be doing it anyway.</p>
      <p>Games got me into computers long before any of that. I've been writing about that history too, from playing DOS games beside my mom to hosting servers for friends. <a href="https://probablyfine.dev/blog/i-just-wanted-to-play-games?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=about" data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">I just wanted to play games</a> is the longer version.</p>
    </div>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection label="Experience" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">Background and tools</h2>
    <p class="measure text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">My work spans Azure platform architecture, networking, Linux, and virtualization, along with the customer-facing work of making the case for a design and getting it approved. <a href="/resume">My resume</a> has the roles and technical detail.</p>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Recognition</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed">
      {recognition.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </DocSection>

  <DocSection label="Say hello" spacing="tight">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 mt-0">Get in touch</h2>
    <p class="measure text-[var(--color-ink-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-4">If there's a project or a role you think I'd be a good fit for, I'd like to hear about it.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm">
      <a href="mailto:maxfield.allison@gmail.com" data-umami-event="email-click" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 gap-1.5"><Icon name="email" size={14} /> Email</a>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxfield-allison/" rel="me noopener" data-umami-event="outbound-linkedin" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 gap-1.5"><Icon name="linkedin" size={14} /> LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/maxfieldallison.com" rel="me noopener" data-umami-event="outbound-bluesky" class="inline-flex items-center min-h-11 gap-1.5"><Icon name="bluesky" size={14} /> Bluesky</a>
    </div>
  </DocSection>
</Layout>
